Human Resources Policy Document
1. Introduction
This document is the official and sole source of HR rules for the organization. In case of conflict with verbal instructions or informal practices, this document overrides all others.
Effective date: 1 January 2026
Policy owner: HR Director
________________________________________
2. Equal Employment Opportunity (EEO)
All hiring and employment decisions must follow these rules:
•	Hiring panels must include at least 2 interviewers 
•	A standardized evaluation form (HR-F01) must be completed for every candidate 
•	Any discrimination complaint must be reported within 7 calendar days 
________________________________________
3. Recruitment and Selection
•	Job postings must remain open for minimum 5 working days 
•	Candidates must pass: 
o	1 HR interview 
o	1 technical/role interview 
•	Offer letters expire after 3 days 
•	Background checks are mandatory for all full-time hires 
________________________________________
4. Employee Classification
•	Full-time: 40 hours/week 
•	Part-time: less than 30 hours/week 
•	Contract: fixed duration, no benefits 
•	Temporary: maximum 6 months duration 
________________________________________
5. Onboarding and Orientation
•	Must be completed within 5 working days 
•	Includes: 
o	Policy briefing (2 hours) 
o	IT setup (1 day) 
o	Manager induction meeting (1 hour) 
•	Probation period: 90 days 
________________________________________
6. Code of Conduct
Employees must:
•	Respond to internal communication within 24 hours 
•	Maintain professional language at all times 
•	Avoid conflicts of interest (must be declared within 48 hours) 
________________________________________
7. Working Hours and Attendance
•	Working hours: 8:00 AM – 4:00 PM 
•	Break: 30 minutes 
•	Late policy: 
o	3 late arrivals/month → verbal warning 
o	5 → written warning 
•	Absence without notice for 2 days = disciplinary action 
________________________________________
8. Compensation and Benefits
•	Salaries paid on the 28th of each month 
•	Overtime rate: 1.25× hourly rate 
•	Annual bonus: up to 10% of salary, based on performance rating ≥ 4/5 
•	Health insurance activated after 30 days of employment 
________________________________________
9. Performance Management
•	Reviews occur twice per year (June & December) 
•	Rating scale: 1 to 5 
•	Improvement plan required for rating ≤ 2 
•	Promotion eligibility requires: 
o	Minimum rating: 4 
o	Tenure: 12 months 
________________________________________
10. Training and Development
•	Each employee receives 20 training hours/year 
•	Mandatory training completion deadline: 31 October 
•	Failure results in performance deduction of -1 rating point 
________________________________________
11. Leave Policy
•	Annual leave: 21 working days/year 
•	Sick leave: 
o	Up to 10 days/year (paid) 
o	Medical certificate required after 2 consecutive days 
•	Emergency leave: 3 days/year 
•	Leave requests must be submitted 5 days in advance 
________________________________________
12. Workplace Health and Safety
•	Safety training required every 12 months 
•	Incidents must be reported within 24 hours 
•	Emergency drills conducted twice per year 
________________________________________
13. Anti-Harassment and Anti-Discrimination
•	Complaints must be filed within 14 days 
•	Investigation timeline: 10 working days 
•	Proven violations result in: 
o	First offense: written warning 
o	Second offense: termination 
________________________________________
14. Diversity and Inclusion
•	Each department must maintain at least 30% gender diversity 
•	Annual inclusion survey required with minimum 80% participation 
________________________________________
15. Confidentiality and Data Protection
•	Confidential data must not be shared externally under any circumstance 
•	Breach penalty: 
o	First offense: suspension (5 days) 
o	Second offense: termination 
________________________________________
16. IT and Acceptable Use Policy
•	Personal use of company devices limited to 30 minutes/day 
•	Unauthorized software installation is prohibited 
•	Passwords must be changed every 60 days 
________________________________________
17. Disciplinary Procedures
Steps:
1.	Verbal warning 
2.	Written warning 
3.	Final warning 
4.	Termination 
Each step must be documented within 48 hours
________________________________________
18. Grievance Handling
•	Complaints must be submitted via HR portal (Form HR-G01) 
•	HR response time: 3 working days 
•	Resolution timeline: 10 working days 
________________________________________
19. Termination and Resignation
•	Notice period: 
o	Employees: 30 days 
o	Employer: 30 days 
•	Final settlement processed within 7 days 
•	Exit interview mandatory 
________________________________________
20. Policy Review and Amendments
•	Policy reviewed every 12 months 
•	Changes require approval from: 
o	HR Director 
o	CEO 
•	Employees must acknowledge updates within 5 days
